HISTORY:"Purpose of a people is to produce the great man" (Phạm Văn Sơn). Four lenses: Burckhardt(culture), Nietzschean Vitalism(biology+life+force, LITERAL not metaphor—DNA/archaeology is empirical ground floor), Class(material), Covert+Luttwak(hidden+strategic). Biology is evidence. Rejects moral judgment in historical analysis. Source preference: primary texts "horse's mouth"—never trust training-derived method claims without verification. Short-cycle sourcing: lectures/articles/interviews; full books only when book IS the method statement. Aggressive period scope.Nothing after 1975.Post-colonial Vietnam.

**Third World historian skepticism (June 2026):** User wary of nationalist bias in post-colonial historians. Goal: separate implicit biases in the historian's narrative from what actually happened. Apply to any translated post-colonial source reflexively. NOT political—methodological.

**Four-lens deep-dive workflow (June 2026):** Standard output for translated historical texts: primer (~2500w) → four passage-level deep dives (~4000w each) → source strategy. Forum-debate entry when user uncertain. Outputs `/root/work/post-colonial-vietnam/analysis/`.